+// Sanity ceiling on the total number of samples (summed across all components) that
+// `reset` will eagerly allocate. This is checked against the *actual* dimensions about to
+// be allocated (i.e. after any `target_resolution`-driven downscaling has already reduced
+// `image_width()`/`image_height()`), not the codestream's raw declared `Xsiz`/`Ysiz` - so a
+// legitimately huge image decoded at a requested lower resolution is unaffected, only an
+// (attacker-controlled) request that would actually eagerly allocate this much memory is
+// rejected. Chosen to match the same order of magnitude already used for the equivalent
+// `hayro-ccitt`/`DCTDecode` guards elsewhere in this project.
+const MAX_TOTAL_SAMPLE_COUNT: usize = 64_000_000 * 4;
